pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io::Result<()>
```

**How it works:**
1. Reads the existing `.note` file for `old_id`
2. Validates the file has 4 SEP-delimited parts and the stored id matches `old_id` — returns `NotFound` error otherwise
3. Reconstructs the file content with `new_id` and `new_title`, preserving the pinned flag (`parts[2]`) and body (`parts[3]`) unchanged
4. Writes the new file as `{new_id}.note`
5. Deletes the old `{old_id}.note` file

**Verified:**
- `cargo build` — compiles cleanly
- `cargo test` — all 2 existing tests pass
- After `rename`, `load_all(dir)` will read only the new file (old one deleted), returning the note with `new_id` and `new_title`


